An unstable nuclide $P$ has decay constant $\lambda_{P}$ and decays to form a nuclide $D$. This nuclide $D$ is unstable and decays with decay constant $\lambda_{D}$ to form a stable nuclide $S$. The decay chain is illustrated in Fig. 12.1.

{{figure:figure_12_1}}

The symbols $P$, $D$ and $S$ are not the nuclide symbols.

Initially, a radioactive sample contains only nuclide $P$.

The variation with time $t$ of the number of nuclei of each of the three nuclides in the sample is shown in Fig. 12.2.

{{figure:figure_12_2}}
